  "rationale": "iterative cannot meet the system batch constraint: it produces one result every N+3 cycles, so 32 requests take 32*(N+3) cycles. For any N that meets the 2^-12 accuracy requirement (N>=13), this needs Fmax > 1 GHz, which is infeasible on Artix-7. Therefore I allocate the entire 100-eval budget to unrolled_k, which can meet both the throughput (>=32 MSPS) and batch (<=0.44 us) constraints with k>=4 and N~13-18. The parameter ranges focus on the minimal-area corner (small W, small N, small guards) while still allowing enough k to reduce cycles and enough guard bits/rounding to achieve the required accuracy. This should map the Pareto front between luts_plus_ffs and accuracy_bits under the system constraints."
}

